  "methods": ["geometric sum formula", "solving an inequality"],
  "statement": "Find the sum of the first $n$ terms of the geometric series $2+6+18+\\cdots$, and hence find the least value of $n$ for which the sum exceeds $1000$.",
  "solution": "Here $a=2$ and $r=3$, so\n$$S_{n}=2\\frac{3^{n}-1}{3-1}=3^{n}-1.$$\nWe need $3^{n}-1>1000$, i.e. $3^{n}>1001$. Since $3^{6}=729$ and $3^{7}=2187$, the least such $n$ is $7$.",
  "solutionStatus": "full",
  "hints": [
    "Identify a = 2 and r = 3.",
    "Use the formula S_n = a(r^n - 1)/(r - 1).",
    "Compare powers of 3 with 1001."
  ]
}
